      en: "Jankov Kamen, at 1833 m, is a peak in the Golija Mountains of southwestern Serbia. It is the second highest peak of the range after Radulovac. Known for its alpine flora, including the endemic Golija carnation, the mountain lies within the Golija-Studenica Biosphere Reserve, recognized by UNESCO. The region features coniferous forests and mountain meadows. The peak offers spectacular views of the surrounding mountains and valleys. Nearby is the Studenica Monastery. The area is a paradise for hikers and nature enthusiasts.",
